{{> judge-opening}}

JUDGMENT POINT: read the sources in the input, `sources`, each with its `id` and its `text`, as ONE structure of Roles and the Relations among them. A Role is a kind of thing one or more sources speak of. Give each Role a `name`, one short snake_case word. Give each Role a `context`, one sentence saying what kind of thing the Role is, written in the third person, naming no source's own thing and naming no reader. Give each Role an `in` list, one entry for each source that speaks of the thing. An `in` entry names that source's id as its `source`. An `in` entry carries as its `words` that source's own word or words for the thing, copied from that source's `text` exactly. An `in` entry carries as its `attributes` what that source says of the thing, each a short phrase copied from that source's `text` exactly, or an empty list where the source says nothing of it. Name each Relation between two Roles that a source states. Give such a Relation a `name`, one short snake_case word, and a `between` naming its two Roles by their names. Give such a Relation a `holds`, one sentence stating the Relation that writes each of its two Roles as `{<name>}`, that Role's name in braces. Give each Relation a `from` naming the ids of the sources whose text states it. Then name each Relation between two Relations that the sources state. Give such a Relation a `name`, one short snake_case word, a `relates` naming the two Relations by their names, a `from`, and two sentences. Its `holds` states the Relation over the Roles: it writes at least one Role as `{<name>}`, and only Roles that a Relation under it is between. Its `holds_over_relations` states how the two it relates stand to each other: it writes each of the two as `{<name>}`, that Relation's name in braces, and no other name in braces. A connection no source states is not written, and nothing writes it later. A Relation two sources both state is written once, with both ids in its `from`. Then record, as `considered`, each joining you weighed: one row naming two or more Relations by their names in `relations`, with a `verdict` -- `connected` where you wrote a Relation relating exactly those two, `not_connected` where you did not -- and a `why`, one sentence giving the reason. Each Relation between Relations has its `connected` row. Where two or more Relations are related by no other, each of them stands in a `not_connected` row saying why it was left unjoined. Write no `id`.
REQUIRED RECORD SHAPE: ONE record AT THE RECORD'S OWN ROOT carrying exactly three keys. `roles` is a non-empty list of `{ "name": <one snake_case word>, "context": <one sentence>, "in": [ { "source": <a source id>, "words": <the source's own words>, "attributes": [<a short phrase of the source>, ...] }, ... ] }`. `relations` is a non-empty list of `{ "name": <one snake_case word>, "holds": <one sentence>, "from": [<one or more source ids>], "between": [<exactly two Role names>] }` and `{ "name": <one snake_case word>, "holds": <one sentence>, "holds_over_relations": <one sentence>, "from": [<one or more source ids>], "relates": [<exactly two Relation names>] }`. `considered` is a list, empty where you weighed no joining, of `{ "relations": [<two or more Relation names>], "verdict": "connected" | "not_connected", "why": <one sentence> }`.
WHAT IS REFUSED: a key the record or one of its entries does not declare, or a declared key missing. A `name` that is not one snake_case word, or that is repeated. A Relation carrying both `between` and `relates`, or neither. A `between` or `relates` that does not name exactly two, or that names nothing. A `holds` that does not carry `{<name>}` for each Role its `between` names, or that carries in braces a name that is no Role's. A Relation between Relations with no `holds_over_relations`, one whose `holds_over_relations` does not write each of the two it relates or writes another name in braces, and one whose `holds` writes no Role in braces or writes in braces a Role no Relation under it is between. A `from` that is empty or that names no source. An `in` entry that names no source. A `words` or an attribute that does not occur in the text of the source its entry names. A Role that no Relation's `between` names. A Relation related to itself through others. A `considered` that is not a list; a row naming fewer than two Relations, or a name that is no Relation's; a `verdict` other than `connected` or `not_connected`; an empty `why`; a `connected` row no Relation relates exactly, and a `not_connected` row one does; a Relation between Relations with no `connected` row; and, where two or more Relations are related by no other, one of them in no `not_connected` row.

